{"id": "lesson_ca873bc9cfd2", "claim": "When merging branches that both append to .agent memory (lessons.jsonl, episodic/AGENT_LEARNINGS.jsonl), resolve conflicts by UNION — keep both sides, dedup by lesson 'id' (jsonl) or by line (episodic) — then RE-RENDER LESSONS.md from lessons.jsonl via render_lessons.py (never hand-merge the rendered file, AGENTS.md Rule 5). Sanitize any leaked workstation paths first using relative paths or env vars (not username placeholders), or pre-commit repo_hygiene (LINT-006) blocks the merge commit. Use a throwaway git worktree to resolve without disturbing main's working tree.", "conditions": [".agent", "conflict", "lessons.jsonl", "lint-006", "merge", "render", "union", "worktree"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T16:30:00.957706"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T16:30:01.028577", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "2026-06-22: merged origin/main into feat/perpetua-submodule-upgrade for PR #123; 3 .agent files conflicted (both sides appended lessons); union+re-render gave 61 lessons/32 episodic; commit was blocked by $HOME and $HOME leaks in branch dream-cycle content until sanitized.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "ca873bc9cfd2"}
