{"id": "lesson_da04cbbae68b", "claim": "Never put literal workstation paths ($HOME/...) in any tracked file — docs, scripts, memory, or config. Use relative paths (../../, ../filename), env vars ($OPENCLAW_ROOT, $REPO_ROOT), or ~ tilde. LINT-006 in repo_hygiene.py and CIDF Target Verification both enforce this as a pre-commit hard gate. The same rule applies to AI-generated memory content: use relative paths or strip the parent path tree; do NOT use <user> placeholder (it still exposes the directory structure).", "conditions": ["anti-doxxing", "cidf", "doxxing", "lint-006", "memory", "relative-paths", "repo_hygiene", "tracked-files", "workstation-paths"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T19:33:36.071175"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T19:33:36.122761", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "LINT-006 / CIDF anti-doxxing invariant: literal workstation paths in tracked files expose the developer's username and machine layout to anyone with repo access. Caught multiple times (2026-06-22 PR #123 dream-cycle content had $HOME and $HOME CI and pre-commit both block commits with violations.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "da04cbbae68b"}
{"id": "lesson_409c00dc67ee", "claim": "Email addresses in ALLOWED_GMAIL_COAUTHORS are NEVER checked for non-gmail domains. The gmail_allowed() gate in check_commit_message.sh only runs when the email ends in @gmail.com or @googlemail.com. Any personal domain (e.g. a custom vanity domain) stored in ALLOWED_GMAIL_COAUTHORS will silently fall through to DENIED. Fix: put non-gmail personal/org addresses in ALLOWED_EXACT_COAUTHOR_EMAILS instead.", "conditions": ["allowlist", "attribution", "check_commit_message", "co-authored-by", "email-domain", "git-guard"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T19:37:38.665209"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T19:37:38.702410", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "2026-06-22: <private email identity> was in ALLOWED_GMAIL_COAUTHORS; commits with Co-authored-by: the identity <<private email identity>> were rejected because gmail_allowed() is guarded by *@gmail.com check. Moved to ALLOWED_EXACT_COAUTHOR_EMAILS (case-insensitive tolower match). Fix in orama scripts/git/check_commit_message.sh, synced to PT via sync-attribution-guard-scripts.sh.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "409c00dc67ee"}
{"id": "lesson_456ea361526d", "claim": "When tracked files contain paths that look absolute (OS-specific home-directory path forms, $HOME use relative paths instead (../../, ../) resolved from the file's own location within the repo. Never use username-containing placeholders or env vars that still expose directory structure (workspace-tree env-var path). The filename alone is sufficient when marked local-only; strip the parent path tree entirely. Standard: relative paths from the file's directory, or ~ for home, or $OPENCLAW_ROOT for the repo root. Applies to all tracked files including .agent/memory JSON and markdown.", "conditions": ["doxxing", "memory", "parent-path", "paths", "relative", "tracked-files", "workspace"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T19:45:16.837240"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T19:45:16.887144", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "PR #123 2026-06-22: WORKSPACE.md had OS-specific home-directory path form — even after replacing with %USERPROFILE%\\\\Downloads\\\\..., the subdirectory tree \\\\Downloads\\\\SKILLS.md\\\\ultrathink\\\\ was still identifying. Correct form: ../Cross-Repo-Memory-Seed.md (relative from working/). Placeholder <user> still reveals path structure.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "456ea361526d"}
{"id": "lesson_3dc9dd3b6986", "claim": "datetime.fromtimestamp() returns naive local time — always pass tz=datetime.timezone.utc for UTC-aware output. Subtracting a naive datetime from an aware one raises TypeError. Also: datetime.now() without tz= is naive; use datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc) everywhere timestamps are compared or stored.", "conditions": ["datetime", "naive", "python", "render_lessons", "timestamps", "timezone", "utc"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T20:06:14.005393"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T20:06:14.075486", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "2026-06-22 CodeRabbit PR #123: render_lessons.py fromtimestamp without tz= vs fallback datetime.now(utc) produced mixed naive/aware accepted_at; _age_factor subtracted naive now() from possibly UTC-aware staged_at, causing TypeError. Fixed both.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "3dc9dd3b6986"}
