{"id": "lesson_9851f3606c7d", "claim": "git conflict resolution regex must close all open syntax constructs (arrays, objects) before emitting structural tokens like '} else {'. When extracting HEAD content from a conflict block that ends mid-array (e.g. plistContent = [ ... last-item, with no ].join), the merge output will have a dangling unclosed array. The fix: always verify node --check on the merged branch, not just the local branch. For if/else platform forks, ensure the darwin branch completes the array, closes the try block, and closes the if before the '} else {' for the Linux branch.", "conditions": ["all", "always", "array", "arrays", "before", "block", "branch", "check", "close", "closes", "completes", "conflict", "constructs", "content", "dangling", "darwin", "else", "emitting", "ends", "ensure", "extracting", "fix", "forks", "git", "head", "join", "just", "last-item", "like", "linux", "local", "merge", "merged", "mid-array", "node", "objects", "open", "output", "platform", "plistcontent", "regex", "resolution", "structural", "syntax", "tokens", "try", "unclosed", "verify"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-24T17:04:03.888212"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-24T17:04:03.954742", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "manual via learn.py at 2026-06-24T17:04:03.888653", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "9851f3606c7d"}
{"id": "lesson_d0ecd37438b4", "claim": "When test expects 'must be a non-empty string' but source emits 'must be a string, got <type>', the root cause is an early guard raising before the canonical check. Refactoring: remove the type-specific early guard and let the single unified check ('not isinstance(val, str) or not val') cover both type mismatches and empty values. This produces one canonical error message that both the test and the error message agree on.", "conditions": ["agree", "before", "both", "canonical", "cause", "check", "cover", "early", "emits", "empty", "error", "expects", "got", "guard", "isinstance", "let", "message", "mismatches", "non-empty", "one", "produces", "raising", "refactoring", "remove", "root", "single", "source", "str", "string", "test", "type", "type-specific", "unified", "val", "values"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-24T17:04:09.020742"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-24T17:04:09.069728", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "manual via learn.py at 2026-06-24T17:04:09.021068", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "d0ecd37438b4"}
