{"id": "lesson_fee9305e811e", "claim": "After any uncertain GitHub Contents API write, read the target ref and compare the expected blob before retrying; a new commit SHA or successful transport response is not proof of insertion, and a retry after delayed success can create an empty child commit with the same tree as its parent.", "conditions": ["destination-verification", "empty-commit", "github-contents-api", "idempotency", "periscope-pr-49", "retry", "tree-sha", "uncertain-write"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-02T22:08:49.476053+00:00"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-09-02T22:08:49.548545+00:00", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "Periscope PR #49 provides exact proof: 214b0c03 changed one test file with 45 insertions and produced tree bd81bba7; child faf515e4 repeated the subject but had the identical bd81bba7 tree and zero file delta after a blind retry. This extends existing empty-commit lesson lesson_9fac191b11e1 from automation-authored/no-op commits to API timeout and retry semantics.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "fee9305e811e"}
