{"id": "lesson_9c4f8a7d21be", "claim": "Canonical MiniGraph finalization: the blanket 'ALWAYS create new objects, NEVER mutate existing ones' instruction was located in orama-system/.cursor/rules/common-coding-style.mdc and superseded on PR #333 by boundary-aware mutation semantics. PerpetuaState generations are deeply isolated with model_copy(update=delta, deep=True); MiniGraph remains an intentional mutable construction builder whose compile() creates the detached runtime snapshot; persistent structural sharing is reserved for future versioned GraphSpec; GraphPlugin multicast guarantees identical GraphObservation delivery to every registered plugin while allowing plugin-specific deterministic filtering; R2.4 separately proves delivery integrity, semantic filtering, and plugin-vs-no-plugin final-state parity. The one-scheduler architecture remains CompiledGraph._run() -> GraphObservation -> aobserve()/GraphEvent -> asteps(). GraphSpec validation remains fail-closed in orama-system.", "conditions": [], "evidence_ids": ["orama-system:.cursor/rules/common-coding-style.mdc", "orama-system:docs/v2/59-minigraph-state-mutation-observer-finalization.md", "oramasys/perpetua-core:src/perpetua_core/state.py", "oramasys/perpetua-core:src/tests/graph/plugins/test_observer.py"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-08-28T04:35:00+08:00", "reviewer": "host-agent", "rationale": "Links the final architecture to the earlier MiniGraph memory chain using the supported graduated-candidate linkage field. It preserves the append-only memory rule while separating that targeted historical-record rule from the superseded blanket coding-style mutation ban.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 9.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "9c4f8a7d21be"}
{"id": "lesson_a02049783fb6", "claim": "Never switch a local-execution stdio MCP server to a hosted/HTTP endpoint without explicit authorization. The local-stdio pattern for Exa MCP exists for two documented reasons, not just portability: (1) a shared singleton daemon + Unix-socket bridge lets Claude, orama-system, and Perpetua-Tools all reuse one authenticated exa-mcp-daemon instead of each spawning its own npx child process (lesson c44a4a1a614d, lesson 2c4124092607) -- that sharing pattern only works for locally-spawned stdio servers, never for type:http/hosted ones; (2) a prior lesson (139389f8f016, 2026-07-22) already warned never to hardcode a fixed relative offset or a literal $HOME path to locate a sibling repo in MCP/tool configs, because checkout topology varies across machines -- and that exact mistake recurred on 2026-08-15 anyway ($HOME/code/OpenClaw/orama-system), meaning the original warning wasn't consulted before the change was made.", "conditions": ["exa-daemon-singleton", "hardcoded-sibling-path-recurrence", "hosted-vs-local-mcp", "mcp-server-transport", "unauthorized-agent-change"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-08-15T15:40:00.000000+00:00"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-08-15T15:40:00.100000+00:00", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "PT PR #354's .codex/config.toml exa MCP server was switched from the local shared-daemon stdio pattern to a hosted mcp-remote endpoint (commit 4d968f9e) by an AI agent (a Gemini-family model, per direct HITL identification) without authorization -- breaking the shared-daemon sharing this session's own machine relies on when multiple agents run concurrently. That was then 'fixed' by a different commit (81a841a4) that reverted to local execution but violated the already-on-record lesson_139389f8f016 by hardcoding a personal directory path as a fallback. Both files are now restored to origin/main's original, authorized content (security-revert commit, same branch). Recorded with the accurate mechanism (singleton daemon + Unix-socket bridge for local stdio only, per c44a4a1a614d/2c4124092607) rather than a guessed one, found via gbrain recall before publishing.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "a02049783fb6"}
